Z||000011||Joe Torma||09-06-2001||10:50 AM||||Apparently all you have to do is change the crystal in the speedo.<P>I found this on a website a long time ago....534/max speedo=cystal freq.<P>I haven't tried this yet, so beware!  I did compare 85/120 speedos and look like this should work. <P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/speedo.JPG"> <P>------------------<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/simplesig.gif">  <BR>Did you get your car in my book yet????<BR> <A HREF="http://www.animatedconcepts.com/fierobook.htm" TARGET=_blank>http://www.animatedconcepts.com/fierobook.htm</A> ||||reg||10
Z||000012||fierohoho||09-06-2001||11:01 AM||||So what you're saying Joe is that to turn a "Canadian" 140kph speedo into a "US" 140 MPH speedo I switch, if your formula is right, to a 3.81 something crystal?<P>That would be cool, who would have the crystal I need, Radio Shack?<P>Would that then recalibrate the odometer?<P>------------------<BR>'84 SE 2.5l<BR>'85 Coupe 2.5l now getting a 3800<BR>'86 SE 2.5l<BR>     <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Pennockpic.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000013||Joe Torma||09-06-2001||11:20 AM||||  <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by fierohoho:<BR><B>So what you're saying Joe is that to turn a "Canadian" 140kph speedo into a "US" 140 MPH speedo I switch, if your formula is right, to a 3.81 something crystal?<P>That would be cool, who would have the crystal I need, Radio Shack?<P>Would that then recalibrate the odometer?<P></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>No Idea on the tach.  Got my 2.4576 crystal for almost nothing from RadioShack.com.  The equation was in MPH so it should be right. <BR><p>[This message has been edited by Joe Torma (edited 09-06-2001).]||||reg||1
