Z||000017||fierohoho||09-08-2001||03:27 PM||||Joe, how close would the crystal freq. have to be to work right. I used your formula and came up with a 3.814 freq. and checked the RadioShack site and the closest they had was a 3.686 or a 4.000. <P>Any idea how much that would throw it off?<P>Which one would you use, any thoughts?<P>------------------<BR>'84 SE 2.5l<BR>'85 Coupe 2.5l now getting a 3800<BR>'86 SE 2.5l<BR>      <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Pennockpic.gif">  <p>[This message has been edited by fierohoho (edited 09-08-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000018||DaRkLoRD||09-08-2001||08:21 PM||||Talk to terryk, he sent me a schematic for a circuit that will recalibrate a speedo to any top speed, doesn't need specific crystal oscillators for a set speed. not quite sure how it works though..<P>I'd like a 240kph speedo.. though I don't think a 2.8 would go that fast.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"> maybe a 3800 SC will...<P>------------------<BR>    <A HREF="mailto:steve@fieroproject.com">steve@fieroproject.com</A>    <BR><A HREF="http://www.fieroproject.com" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fieroproject.com</A>||||reg||3
Z||000019||Joe Torma||09-08-2001||08:27 PM||||  <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by fierohoho:<BR><B>Joe, how close would the crystal freq. have to be to work right. I used your formula and came up with a 3.814 freq. and checked the RadioShack site and the closest they had was a 3.686 or a 4.000. <P>Any idea how much that would throw it off?<P>Which one would you use, any thoughts?<P></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P><BR>Now my head hurts.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smiley_drunk.gif">   I figured out the speed differences across the range.  You are limited with what crystals are available.  Remember, tire size and speedo gears throw new variables in here. Bold #s are speedo max speeds and italic are your crystals.  Once again, I haven't installed and tired mine yet.<P>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/sppedo.gif">  <P>------------------<BR>    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/simplesig.gif">   <BR>Did you get your car in my book yet????<BR> <A HREF="http://www.animatedconcepts.com/fierobook.htm" TARGET=_blank>http://www.animatedconcepts.com/fierobook.htm</A> <p>[This message has been edited by Joe Torma (edited 09-08-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000020||fierohoho||09-11-2001||12:07 AM||||Joe, thanks for the formula.<P>I picked up a 3.686 crystal today and plan on installing it in my 140Kmh speedo Wednesday.<P>That should convert it to a 140MPH speedo except for the metric markings.<P>I'm going to borrow a spare radar unit from work to check the accuracy. I'll run a thread in the tech section on the outcome with speedo/radar comparisons. <P>Hope to have it done and tested by the 17th.<P>I think then I will pickup the 4.00 crystal and test it the same way at a later time and post those results.<P>------------------<BR>'84 SE 2.5l<BR>'85 Coupe 2.5l now getting a 3800<BR>'86 SE 2.5l<BR>     <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Pennockpic.gif"> ||||reg||1
